.TH SH-MESH 1
.SH NAME
mesh \- shell script interface to mesh(2)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B load mesh

.B ${mesh
.I NXxNY
.RB [ domain
.IR WxH ]
.RB [ bc
.IR clamp|periodic|zero ]
.B }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mesh
is a loadable module for
.IR sh (1)
giving shell scripts direct access to
.IR mesh (2)'s
own little language for describing a grid, without going through a
larger consumer like
.IR sh-pde (1).
.PP
.B ${mesh}
parses its arguments exactly as
.IR mesh (2)'s
.B parse
does, and yields five elements: the grid's
.IR nx ,
.IR ny ,
.IR dx ,
and
.I dy
followed by the boundary mode as one of the words
.BR clamp ,
.BR periodic ,
or
.BR zero .
A caller typically destructures the result directly:
.EX
	(nx ny dx dy bc) = ${mesh 64x64 domain 1x1 bc periodic}
.EE
A malformed spec raises a
.B mesh
exception carrying the same error text
.IR mesh (2)'s
.B parse
would have returned.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/sh/mesh.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR mesh (2),
.IR sh (1),
.IR sh-pde (1)
